      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Key Service**\n\nI'm zeroing in on defining a key service, and I'm leaning toward selecting a concrete external provider. The goal is to make this choice explicit in the code for envelope encryption. I'm also considering the use of a data encryption key (DEK) as a standard practice for envelope encryption.\n\n\n**Selecting a Specific Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud KMS as the managed key service. The Python code will leverage the `google-cloud-kms` library for all operations, including DEK generation and encryption/decryption, thus making the provider explicit. The file, `envelope_encrypt.py`, is underway, structuring the functions needed for generating, encrypting, and decrypting data. I will structure the code to include Google Cloud KMS-specific imports.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789864074911,
          "start": 1789864071259
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc36505b001SwNkxpCBYA2JZ4",
